    "body": "Couple small questions I have:\r\n\r\n - When is it correct to use a `<span>` vs `<code data-x>` vs `<a>`? In whatwg/console we use `<a>` a lot to reference definitions, and this is outlined a bit in the bikeshed spec too. I notice here we seem to use `<span>` (for example \"being rendered\") and `<code data-x>` in some possibly special situations.\r\n - What exactly does the `data-x` attribute represent (on `code` for example) and why do we use it?\r\n - What is the purpose of `<div node-v`>? As in, what does this attribute signify and how many things should go inside of this kind of div?\r\n\r\nIt's possible the answers to all these questions are conveniently located somewhere that I simply overlooked so if that is the case, my bad!",
