    "body": "So, the rearranging seems to have broken the display: contents case, wherein a node can have no CSS boxes (i.e. is not \"being rendered\") but still has children that are being rendered. This is noted in the old spec as\r\n\r\n> items can be non-empty due to 'display:contents'.\r\n\r\nBut in the new spec, where that note appears, items is always empty.\r\n\r\nBasically I think step 3 of the inner text collection steps needs to move back up. In general the steps got reordered a bit. Let me put them back, then you can check my reasoning.",
